 "pg_test_fsync_raw": "5 seconds per test\nO_DIRECT supported on this platform for open_datasync and open_sync.\n\nCompare file sync methods using one 8kB write:\n(in \"wal_sync_method\" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)\n        open_datasync                      5005.189 ops/sec     200 usecs/op\n        fdatasync                          5119.723 ops/sec     195 usecs/op\n        fsync                              5102.016 ops/sec     196 usecs/op\n        fsync_writethrough                              n/a\n        open_sync                          5097.082 ops/sec     196 usecs/op\n\nCompare file sync methods using two 8kB writes:\n(in \"wal_sync_method\" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)\n        open_datasync                      4769.072 ops/sec     210 usecs/op\n        fdatasync                          5004.242 ops/sec     200 usecs/op\n        fsync                              5022.938 ops/sec     199 usecs/op\n        fsync_writethrough                              n/a\n        open_sync                          4707.271 ops/sec     212 usecs/op\n\nCompare open_sync with different write sizes:\n(This is designed to compare the cost of writing 16kB in different write\nopen_sync sizes.)\n         1 * 16kB open_sync write          5081.071 ops/sec     197 usecs/op\n         2 *  8kB open_sync writes         4666.944 ops/sec     214 usecs/op\n         4 *  4kB open_sync writes         2997.874 ops/sec     334 usecs/op\n         8 *  2kB open_sync writes          154.228 ops/sec    6484 usecs/op\n        16 *  1kB open_sync writes           46.228 ops/sec   21632 usecs/op\n\nTest if fsync on non-write file descriptor is honored:\n(If the times are similar, fsync() can sync data written on a different\ndescriptor.)\n        write, fsync, close                3963.606 ops/sec     252 usecs/op\n        write, close, fsync                4323.476 ops/sec     231 usecs/op\n\nNon-sync'ed 8kB writes:\n        write                            935083.411 ops/sec       1 usecs/op\n",
